WEBVTT

00:01.835 --> 00:03.132
Kandi, Kandi, listen to me.

00:03.303 --> 00:05.737
Our divorce does not
have to be adversarial.

00:06.039 --> 00:07.631
Bet she won't know that word.

00:08.374 --> 00:10.672
No, not ads for cereal.

00:12.612 --> 00:14.739
- Told you.
- Do you know it?

00:15.115 --> 00:16.446
That wasrt the bet.

00:17.383 --> 00:21.911
Oh, come on, you're being very unfair.
I love Chester as much as you do.

00:22.088 --> 00:24.079
Oh. Oh, really? Then maybe
you can explain to me...

00:24.257 --> 00:27.249
...why I'm the one who feeds Chester,
gives Chester tick baths...

00:27.427 --> 00:29.520
...and cleans up
when Chester piddles on the rug.

00:30.029 --> 00:31.929
When did you change your name
to Chester?

00:35.769 --> 00:37.794
It's not just me. Jake loves that dog too.

00:38.138 --> 00:39.264
No, I don't.

00:41.040 --> 00:43.474
He slobbers and he threw up in my shoe.

00:43.943 --> 00:46.104
I had a date like that once.

00:46.880 --> 00:49.678
You think it would've slowed me down,
but no.

00:50.016 --> 00:51.813
All right. Can I at least talk to him?

00:52.152 --> 00:56.054
My father talks to dogs
and they send me to a psychologist.

00:56.222 --> 00:57.712
Hello, Chester?

00:57.891 --> 01:00.189
It's Daddy.

01:00.360 --> 01:02.328
Who's a good boy?

01:02.495 --> 01:04.122
You're a good boy.

01:04.564 --> 01:07.431
Yes, you are. Yes, you are.

01:07.600 --> 01:10.160
Yes, you... Kandi, I wasrt finished.

01:10.703 --> 01:12.466
Yeah, well, I have rights here.

01:12.639 --> 01:16.632
And I intend to pursue those rights
with all the means at my disposal.

01:16.810 --> 01:19.335
Yeah. Well, okay. Okay. Goodbye.

01:21.815 --> 01:23.510
- Alan?
- Yeah?

01:23.683 --> 01:27.983
Who's a moron? You're a moron.
Yes, you are. Yes, you are.

01:29.689 --> 01:34.092
Well, it may be funny to you,
but that dog means a lot to me.

01:34.594 --> 01:38.086
- This about the dog or is it about Kandi?
- It's about the dog.

01:38.264 --> 01:40.789
I mean, we bought a condo.
She's keeping it.

01:40.967 --> 01:43.629
We bought a car. She's keeping it.
What do I get to keep?

01:43.803 --> 01:45.236
Certainly not your dignity.

01:47.941 --> 01:50.034
Okay, let's look at the big picture.

01:50.210 --> 01:53.304
You're a middle-aged guy who married
a stupid woman half his age...

01:53.479 --> 01:56.937
...for no other reason than the sex
was great. You with me so far?

01:57.116 --> 01:58.777
- Yeah.
- Good.

01:58.952 --> 02:01.853
Then you ran out of money,
she got bored and threw you out.

02:02.488 --> 02:04.956
- What's your point?
- Why does everything need a point?

02:05.124 --> 02:07.217
Why can't I just make fun of you?

02:08.928 --> 02:10.361
I want my dog, Charlie.

02:10.530 --> 02:13.761
There will be other dogs.
Not in my house.

02:15.869 --> 02:19.396
Just remember, the worst thing you can do
is fight over who gets what.

02:19.572 --> 02:21.938
- The trick is to give her everything.
- Everything?

02:22.108 --> 02:24.338
Whatever she wants.
When all is said and done...

02:24.510 --> 02:28.412
...you'll get the thing that matters most.
The thing you can't put a price on.

02:28.581 --> 02:31.982
- My dignity?
- Oh, stop it. That ship has sailed.

02:34.087 --> 02:37.648
No, no, no, the thing you get is freedom.

02:37.824 --> 02:39.758
The opportunity to start over.

02:39.926 --> 02:42.451
Maybe a little sadder,
but a whole lot wiser.

02:42.629 --> 02:45.291
The next time you meet a woman...
And trust me, you will.

02:45.465 --> 02:49.424
- You'll have a real shot
at true and lasting happiness.

02:50.470 --> 02:53.166
I want my dog.

02:55.308 --> 02:58.744
Well, good luck with that because
I was lying about the other stuff.

03:27.607 --> 03:29.507
Why don't we share custody of Chester?

03:29.676 --> 03:32.372
You know, you get one week
and I get one week.

03:32.812 --> 03:34.973
It doesn't make any difference.

03:35.381 --> 03:39.044
Dog weeks and people weeks
are the same thing.

03:41.688 --> 03:44.020
Hey, Dad, how come
you don't give me an allowance?

03:44.190 --> 03:47.057
Your mother gives you an allowance.
I'm trying to be fair.

03:47.226 --> 03:51.219
Speaking of fair, it doesn't seem fair
that Mom has to pay me and you don't.

03:51.965 --> 03:54.365
Hang on, Kandi.
Let me explain something to you.

03:54.534 --> 03:56.593
Every cent your mother has
comes from me.

03:56.769 --> 03:59.761
So when she gives you allowance,
it's me giving you allowance.

03:59.939 --> 04:03.340
I don't need to know how it works.
I just need more money.

04:06.212 --> 04:07.236
Take a number.

04:07.613 --> 04:09.547
- Sorry, go ahead.
- Six.

04:13.786 --> 04:16.152
- Morning.
- Morning.

04:16.322 --> 04:20.053
If Chester's gonna live anywhere full time,
I don't see why it shouldn't be here.

04:20.226 --> 04:22.251
I do. I see why.

04:24.230 --> 04:27.256
When he split with your mother,
did they fight over your custody?

04:27.433 --> 04:30.527
They still do. "You take him. "
"No, you take him. "

04:31.237 --> 04:34.138
Okay. Okay. Okay, fine.
You want this to get ugly?

04:34.307 --> 04:37.242
You wanna play hardball?
I will play hardball.

04:37.643 --> 04:41.739
- How come you don't give me an allowance?
- What are you, drunk?

04:41.914 --> 04:44.610
Well... Yeah, well,
I am gonna get a lawyer.

04:44.784 --> 04:48.811
I'm gonna take you to court, yeah,
and then we'll just see who gets Chester.

04:48.988 --> 04:51.923
Yeah. Yeah. Well, have your lawyer
call my lawyer.

05:02.068 --> 05:04.002
You know a lawyer?

05:12.712 --> 05:14.009
Oh.

05:14.747 --> 05:16.578
- Hi.
- What do you want, Alan?

05:17.350 --> 05:19.944
Uh, oh, okay, right to it, huh?

05:20.119 --> 05:23.748
Uh, well, as you know,
Kandi and I are splitting up.

05:23.923 --> 05:26.414
&lt;i>Yeah, quelle surprise.&lt;/i>

05:29.695 --> 05:33.825
Uh... Anyhoo,
I'm gonna need a good lawyer...

05:34.000 --> 05:37.527
...and I thought, you know,
who better than the rabid jackal...

05:37.703 --> 05:40.331
...who ripped my lungs out
in my first divorce?

05:40.973 --> 05:42.099
You want my lawyer?

05:42.275 --> 05:44.505
Well, I certainly don't want mine.

05:45.278 --> 05:47.439
Gee, I'm sorry,
but I can't give him to you.

05:47.613 --> 05:50.275
- Why not?
- Because I already gave him to Kandi.

05:51.117 --> 05:52.641
You're joking, right?

05:53.019 --> 05:56.045
No, I'm smiling, but I'm not joking.

05:57.190 --> 05:58.521
Why would you do that?

05:58.825 --> 06:01.157
I don't know. Kicks.

06:01.761 --> 06:04.787
Oh, Judith, when did you start
hating me so much?

06:04.964 --> 06:08.297
Well, let's see.
I disliked you when we were married.

06:08.468 --> 06:11.460
I resented you when we divorced.
But I don't think I hated you...

06:11.637 --> 06:15.403
...until you started having sex
with that gorgeous 22-year-old dumbbell.

06:16.075 --> 06:19.272
- Okay, well, thanks for clearing that up.
- Okay, bye-bye.

06:23.583 --> 06:25.847
Look, if you really wanna make some
extra cash...

06:26.018 --> 06:28.077
...we can find some chores
for you to do.

06:28.254 --> 06:30.347
Oh, yeah, there's big money in that.

06:32.458 --> 06:33.925
What kind of chores?

06:34.260 --> 06:35.591
Well, let's see.

06:35.761 --> 06:38.992
You could take out the garbage,
sweep up the garage, wash my car.

06:39.265 --> 06:41.825
No, none of those sound good.

06:45.104 --> 06:47.038
Tell you what.

06:48.741 --> 06:50.868
I'll give you 10 bucks...

06:51.043 --> 06:54.342
...if you can eat this entire tub
of ice cream in less than 20 minutes.

06:54.514 --> 06:57.381
- Okay.
- Charlie, that'll shoot out of him...

06:57.550 --> 07:00.485
...like Ben &amp; Jerry on rocket skates.

07:01.087 --> 07:03.954
Here. Eat these instead.

07:04.123 --> 07:07.752
By the time they get through you,
it will be your mother's problem.

07:08.928 --> 07:11.419
- All of them in 20 minutes, right?
- Yep.

07:11.597 --> 07:13.292
Then can I have the ice cream?

07:16.269 --> 07:17.531
Uh-oh.

07:30.216 --> 07:32.411
Alan, you should've called.

07:32.585 --> 07:34.780
I didn't feel like calling.
I wanna see my dog.

07:34.954 --> 07:36.717
Well, maybe he doesn't wanna see you.

07:37.223 --> 07:40.886
- Why don't we let him decide?
- No, he's been through enough.

07:41.527 --> 07:43.051
Oh, really? Did he tell you that?

07:43.462 --> 07:45.054
How could he tell me anything?

07:45.231 --> 07:48.564
You know as well as I do
that he keeps everything bottled up.

07:49.068 --> 07:52.504
- Damn it, Kandi, I wanna see my...
- Don't you yell at me.

07:52.672 --> 07:54.970
If you have anything to say,
say it to my lawyer.

07:55.141 --> 07:56.472
Maybe I will.

07:56.642 --> 07:59.338
Honey, Alan has something
he wants to say to you.

08:01.480 --> 08:03.141
Hey, Alan.

08:04.450 --> 08:05.781
What's up?

08:08.287 --> 08:10.187
It's you.

08:10.456 --> 08:11.582
The jackal.

08:13.392 --> 08:15.257
Oh, that hurts. Ahem.

08:15.428 --> 08:19.194
Listen, as long as you're here,
is your billing address still the same?

08:19.832 --> 08:20.890
Uh-huh.

08:21.067 --> 08:23.160
Great. Well, I guess I'll see you in court.

08:24.470 --> 08:27.496
Oh. And don't worry. I'm not gonna
bill you for this consultation.

08:27.940 --> 08:29.874
There's nothing legal going on here.

08:37.583 --> 08:40.450
Un-freaking-believable.

08:40.953 --> 08:43.547
It's like watching a pot-smoking monkey.

08:44.357 --> 08:48.020
- Ten dollars, please.
- Serves me right betting against a kid...

08:48.194 --> 08:50.162
...who can eat a Happy Meal,
toys and all.

08:52.064 --> 08:53.793
Thank you.

08:54.300 --> 08:57.792
- What are you doing?
- You taught me always do my own count.

08:57.970 --> 08:59.369
Yeah, but you can trust me.

08:59.939 --> 09:04.171
Seven, eight, nine?

09:06.379 --> 09:08.711
It was an honest mistake.

09:09.215 --> 09:10.477
I'm sure.

09:12.585 --> 09:14.644
So, what are you gonna do
with your winnings?

09:14.820 --> 09:17.084
- It's a secret.
- So it's a girl.

09:17.256 --> 09:18.883
- How did you know?
- I didn't.

09:19.058 --> 09:20.389
Then it isn't.

09:22.028 --> 09:24.087
Come on. Tell me about her.
Maybe I can help.

09:24.463 --> 09:25.691
I don't think so.

09:25.865 --> 09:29.062
Are you kidding? Who knows
more about girls than your Uncle Charlie?

09:29.235 --> 09:31.669
Warren Beatty, Bill Clinton,
Rosie o'Donnell.

09:34.907 --> 09:38.843
Why should I talk to you? You've messed
up every relationship you've ever been in.

09:39.011 --> 09:40.069
Well, yeah...

09:40.246 --> 09:43.238
- So you're not exactly a good example.
- I get it.

09:43.416 --> 09:45.350
If I were old enough
to have one-night stands...

09:45.518 --> 09:47.577
All right, you've made your point.

09:47.753 --> 09:49.687
- So don't talk to me. Okay.
- I won't.

09:49.855 --> 09:51.584
- Okay.
- Good.

09:56.896 --> 09:59.558
- Will you drive me to the mall?
- Why?

09:59.799 --> 10:03.098
- It's private.
- So is my car.

10:04.437 --> 10:06.462
All right, I wanna buy a present.

10:06.872 --> 10:09.136
- For?
- It's a secret.

10:09.308 --> 10:11.708
- I'll throw in another 10.
- Wendy Cho.

10:12.044 --> 10:13.033
Aha.

10:13.212 --> 10:15.203
A present for Wendy Cho.

10:15.548 --> 10:19.040
Now, is this an offering to grease
the wheels or a parting gift...

10:19.218 --> 10:21.311
...for the wheels
having already been greased?

10:21.620 --> 10:25.750
Grease the wheels? See, that's
why I don't talk to you about this stuff.

10:27.927 --> 10:30.657
Well, he may be as dull
as a butter knife...

10:30.830 --> 10:34.061
...but you got to admit,
he's a good judge of character.

10:45.010 --> 10:47.877
Are you sure it doesn't have anything
to do with sex?

10:48.047 --> 10:49.605
- Positive.
- Huh.

10:49.782 --> 10:54.048
Sure sounds like it. Subpoenas.

11:02.628 --> 11:05.028
Hang in there, Chester. Daddy's coming.

11:05.197 --> 11:07.290
Oh, please, please, please.

11:08.768 --> 11:11.498
Yes, she didn't change the lock.

11:16.542 --> 11:18.669
But that's new.

11:21.706 --> 11:23.765
I like those.

11:23.941 --> 11:25.568
Skull earrings?

11:25.943 --> 11:28.503
Yeah, they're silver
and they got ruby eyes.

11:29.080 --> 11:32.675
Okay, first of all,
for 11.95 those aren't rubies.

11:32.850 --> 11:36.013
- You don't know that.
- Oh, but I do.

11:37.421 --> 11:40.822
And second, girls like Wendy Cho
don't wear skull earrings.

11:40.992 --> 11:42.118
How do you know?

11:42.293 --> 11:44.523
She gets straight A's, right?
She plays violin?

11:44.695 --> 11:47.255
- She's also the captain of the math team.
- Exactly.

11:47.431 --> 11:50.264
- So you see my point?
- Oh, okay.

11:52.370 --> 11:55.066
How about that skull belt buckle?

11:56.474 --> 11:58.908
No skulls.

11:59.277 --> 12:03.179
Just out of curiosity,
does this Wendy Cho hate her parents?

12:03.347 --> 12:04.780
I don't think so. Why?

12:04.949 --> 12:07.440
Just trying to get a handle
on the relationship.

12:08.052 --> 12:10.885
She says she likes me
because I'm unpretentious.

12:11.055 --> 12:14.354
- Do you know what that means?
- It means she likes me.

12:15.359 --> 12:17.327
Yeah, okay.

12:17.495 --> 12:19.463
So, what do you want this gift to say?

12:19.630 --> 12:20.619
Uh...

12:20.798 --> 12:21.890
Happy birthday?

12:22.066 --> 12:24.000
A birthday card says "happy birthday. "

12:24.168 --> 12:26.636
What are you trying to tell her
by giving her jewelry?

12:26.804 --> 12:29.830
I don't know. I guess that I love her.

12:31.208 --> 12:32.675
What?

12:32.843 --> 12:34.640
Nothing. That's terrific.

12:34.812 --> 12:37.645
Because you don't love any girl,
doesn't mean I shouldn't.

12:38.215 --> 12:42.083
Excuse me, but I have loved many girls
and many girls have loved me.

12:42.253 --> 12:43.914
That's not love. It's just sex.

12:45.623 --> 12:48.183
I'm sorry, I'm not following you.

12:48.859 --> 12:51.885
If you died tomorrow,
how many girls would come to your funeral?

12:52.063 --> 12:53.758
A lot of them.

12:53.931 --> 12:57.833
Granted, a few might show up
just to make sure I'm really dead...

12:58.336 --> 13:00.395
...but I feel confident...

13:00.571 --> 13:05.770
...that the overall tone of the event
would be one of sadness.

13:06.610 --> 13:09.340
- Lf you say so.
- Yeah, I say so.

13:10.047 --> 13:13.016
- Now let's get out of here.
- I haven't picked out a gift yet.

13:13.184 --> 13:15.448
Then get her the stupid skull earrings.

13:15.619 --> 13:19.055
- But you said she wouldn't like them.
- What do I know? Nobody loves me.

13:19.223 --> 13:21.282
Nobody's coming to my funeral.

13:21.659 --> 13:24.127
Whoa, where did that come from?

13:27.865 --> 13:31.460
Here, what about
this gold heart necklace?

13:32.737 --> 13:34.534
It's kind of expensive.

13:34.705 --> 13:36.536
You want the best, Jake,
you pay for it.

13:37.041 --> 13:42.775
Yeah, but $39?
I mean, I love her and everything...

13:43.414 --> 13:46.872
If it means we can get out
of here quicker, I'll front you the difference.

13:47.284 --> 13:50.412
- I don't know.
- You don't know? I'm offering you a deal.

13:50.588 --> 13:54.490
Yeah, but you always say if it sounds
too good to be true, it probably is.

13:54.658 --> 13:57.149
All right, how about if I pay
for the whole thing?

13:57.561 --> 14:00.155
That sounds even better. So no.

14:01.766 --> 14:03.893
Come on, brainiac.

14:04.668 --> 14:06.693
What do I have to do for you?

14:06.871 --> 14:08.805
Just promise to be sad at my funeral.

14:08.973 --> 14:10.736
- Do I have to cry?
- No.

14:10.908 --> 14:12.842
Will there be food?

14:13.277 --> 14:14.904
- Yes.
- Can I bring a date?

14:17.782 --> 14:21.309
- You're just screwing with me now, right?
- How does it feel?

14:26.757 --> 14:28.691
Still early. Wanna go shoot some hoops?

14:28.859 --> 14:31.521
No, I'm gonna go call Wendy Cho.

14:32.963 --> 14:36.057
Hey, bros before Chos.

14:39.870 --> 14:42.862
"Thanks for the ride to the mall,
Uncle Charlie.

14:43.741 --> 14:47.700
Thanks for buying me the necklace,
Uncle Charlie. Thanks for not slugging me...

14:47.878 --> 14:51.473
...when I started mouthing off
about your funeral, Uncle Charlie. "

15:13.871 --> 15:14.929
Aah!

15:22.513 --> 15:23.810
Chester...

15:23.981 --> 15:25.039
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

15:25.216 --> 15:26.308
Calm down.

15:26.650 --> 15:28.641
Easy, boy.
Charlie, what did you do to him?

15:28.819 --> 15:32.983
What did I do to him? I practically
crapped my pants is what I did to him.

15:33.157 --> 15:37.116
- What the hell is that?
- This is Chester. Isn't he cute? Yes, you are.

15:37.294 --> 15:39.660
- Yes, you are. Yes...
- He's not staying here, Alan.

15:40.464 --> 15:42.932
With all due respect,
that's what you said about me.

15:43.868 --> 15:47.326
That's because no kennel in town
would take you.

15:47.505 --> 15:48.904
Oh, come on, look at him.

15:49.073 --> 15:51.507
- How can you not love this face?
- Easy.

15:51.675 --> 15:53.973
I know where he puts it.

15:54.144 --> 15:57.011
- Now take him back to Kandi's.
- I can't.

15:57.181 --> 15:59.274
- Why not?
- It's kind of complicated.

15:59.450 --> 16:02.544
- Then simplify it.
- Okay, well, um...

16:02.720 --> 16:05.018
...I stole him.

16:06.690 --> 16:11.218
Oh, Alan, I may think with my penis
but at least I think.

16:11.529 --> 16:14.293
You won't have to do anything.
I'll feed him, I'll walk him.

16:14.698 --> 16:19.032
Walk him? You could hitch a wagon
to him and settle the West.

16:20.204 --> 16:22.035
No dogs in my house.

16:22.206 --> 16:25.801
Especially stolen dogs who are big enough
to make me their bitch.

16:26.477 --> 16:29.207
Whoa, what the hell is that?

16:29.613 --> 16:31.046
That is leaving.

16:31.215 --> 16:34.548
Please. My entire life, Chester
is the only thing I ever slept with...

16:34.718 --> 16:36.549
...that didn't sue me for alimony.

16:37.721 --> 16:40.155
How long you think
you're gonna get away with this?

16:40.324 --> 16:43.691
I was very careful. I left the door open
so that when Kandi comes home...

16:43.861 --> 16:46.352
...she'll think she left it open
and Chester ran away.

16:46.530 --> 16:48.430
She'll never dream
of looking for him here.

16:50.234 --> 16:51.861
Probably.

16:53.170 --> 16:55.570
Just in case, hide Chester.

16:56.507 --> 16:58.441
How am I supposed to hide him?

16:58.609 --> 17:01.009
Sit under him with a pail
and pretend he's a cow.

17:03.080 --> 17:06.914
- Coming. Charlie, please.
- Oh, man.

17:07.318 --> 17:08.876
Come on, Bullwinkle.

17:18.929 --> 17:20.123
Alan Harper?

17:20.764 --> 17:23.255
Yes. Yes. How can I help you?

17:23.434 --> 17:25.800
We're investigating a stolen-dog report.

17:25.970 --> 17:27.096
A dog?

17:27.805 --> 17:29.830
Your ex-wife's dog.

17:30.407 --> 17:32.807
Chester? Somebody stole Chester?

17:34.311 --> 17:37.109
She seems to think you might know
his whereabouts.

17:37.748 --> 17:42.310
Oh, gosh, um, I'm sorry.
I have no idea.

17:42.486 --> 17:45.455
Uh... oh, although, you know,
what could've happened...

17:45.623 --> 17:48.615
...um, she could have
left the door open...

17:48.792 --> 17:52.193
She's absent-minded.
- Uh, and the dog got away.

17:53.764 --> 17:56.460
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

18:13.350 --> 18:14.977
Hey.

18:15.386 --> 18:18.082
Oh, look who's finally off the phone.

18:18.255 --> 18:19.847
Yeah.

18:20.224 --> 18:22.385
When are you gonna give Wendy Cho
the necklace?

18:22.559 --> 18:23.583
I'm not.

18:24.561 --> 18:26.358
What happened? You chicken out?

18:26.730 --> 18:28.288
No.

18:29.366 --> 18:31.061
I don't believe it.

18:31.235 --> 18:33.499
You dragged my ass
all the way down to the mall...

18:33.671 --> 18:36.663
...I pony up 40 bucks for the necklace,
and you chicken out.

18:36.840 --> 18:39.673
She just dumped me, you old turd.

18:42.680 --> 18:47.344
Oh. Well, you could've told me that
before I started being a turd.

18:47.518 --> 18:51.079
I'm only 12. I need a time machine.

18:52.523 --> 18:55.458
Ah, dude, I am really sorry.
What happened?

18:55.626 --> 18:59.460
She decided she has a problem
with mixed relationships.

19:01.398 --> 19:03.764
What? Chinese and Caucasian?

19:04.268 --> 19:06.566
Gifted and remedial.

19:08.205 --> 19:09.866
Oh.

19:10.140 --> 19:13.735
Yeah, well, I'm done with relationships.
From now on, I'm gonna be like you.

19:14.344 --> 19:16.005
Why would you wanna be like me?

19:16.180 --> 19:20.082
Because you never fall in love
with anybody, so you never get hurt.

19:20.951 --> 19:23.715
Okay, listen to me.

19:25.322 --> 19:27.256
Being hurt sucks...

19:27.424 --> 19:31.622
...but love is the most beautiful
and noble of human emotions.

19:31.795 --> 19:35.822
It's what gives a man hope.
It's what gives his life meaning.

19:35.999 --> 19:37.967
Don't turn your back on love, Jake.

19:38.135 --> 19:41.502
I did and I regret it every day.

19:42.206 --> 19:45.403
- Really?
- May God strike me down if I'm lying.

19:57.187 --> 19:59.985
All right, the game's over. Let's go.

20:00.157 --> 20:01.590
Where are we going?

20:01.759 --> 20:04.523
Might as well bail your dad out of jail.

20:07.164 --> 20:08.791
Can we get something to eat first?

20:08.966 --> 20:10.900
Sure, why not.

20:15.439 --> 20:19.273
How long before Kandi
and her lawyer come back from Mexico?

20:20.210 --> 20:22.110
Three more days.

20:23.647 --> 20:26.343
Oh, God, what are you feeding that dog?

20:26.517 --> 20:28.781
It's not the dog.

20:29.753 --> 20:32.051
Smells a little like banana bread.
